        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of using a modified merge sort to count inversions, consider using a Fenwick Tree (Binary Indexed Tree) to efficiently count and update the number of inversions during the sorting process. This approach allows for an optimal solution with a time complexity of O(n log n).",
